strings.VOR_destination_fief_of_the_region_categ:
As the state expands its control over the fragmented Motherland, Secretary Blokhin and his supporters are implementing their own vision of collectivization. According to this vision, one of two wings of local government must be established in every district. These separate regional authorities must be affiliated with the Communist Party and have 2 to 4 years of administrative or combat experience.

When appointing governors from their inner circle, they choose either trusted military groups—most of whom are NKVD—or civilian officials who obediently carry out all instructions from the party apparatus and personally from the secretary. In general, they share one common trait—hostility toward the urban non-working class, namely consumers who merely consume finished products supplied from the countryside. In fact, they are given a choice from Military Commissariats: either enlist in the army for a term of 4 years or work for the unlimited duration in the fields in the countryside. Or, at the initiative of the civilian Collective Farms, to work diligently in the agricultural sector for several years, as long as the Union's self-sufficiency requires it.

These two factions exist in a precarious balance, often failing to agree on the assignment of a particular district. Our task in maintaining order and preventing unrest in the state is to preserve the balance between their assigned territories. Perhaps, at times, it will be appropriate to leave districts important to us without designated control altogether..

